    {
      "scene_no": 3,
      "template_id": "math_derivation",
      "teacher_script": "First, let's calculate the perimeter of the square field. A square has four equal sides, so its perimeter is simply four times the length of one side. With a side of 60 meters, the square's perimeter is 240 meters.",
      "template_data": {
        "equation_steps": [
          "Perimeter of Square = 4 × Side",
          "Perimeter of Square = 4 × 60 m",
          "Perimeter of Square = 240 m"
        ],
        "animation_style": "stagger_in"
      },
      "audio_url": "./scene_3.wav"
    },
    {
      "scene_no": 4,
      "template_id": "math_derivation",
      "teacher_script": "Now, we know the rectangular field has the same perimeter: 240 meters. The formula for a rectangle's perimeter is 2 times (length + width). We have the length, so we can solve for the unknown width.",
      "template_data": {
        "equation_steps": [
          "Perimeter of Rectangle = 2 × (Length + Width)",
          "240 m = 2 × (80 m + Width)",
          "120 m = 80 m + Width",
          "Width = 120 m - 80 m",
          "Width = 40 m"
        ],
        "animation_style": "stagger_in"
      },
      "audio_url": "./scene_4.wav"
    },
    {
      "scene_no": 5,
      "template_id": "math_derivation",
      "teacher_script": "With all dimensions known, let's calculate the area. The area of a square is found by multiplying the side length by itself. For our 60-meter square, this gives us 3600 square meters.",
      "template_data": {
        "equation_steps": [
          "Area of Square = Side × Side",
          "Area of Square = 60 m × 60 m",
          "Area of Square = 3600 m²"
        ],
        "animation_style": "stagger_in"
      },
      "audio_url": "./scene_5.wav"
    },
    {
      "scene_no": 6,
      "template_id": "math_derivation",
      "teacher_script": "Next, we calculate the area of the rectangular field. We now know its length is 80 meters and its width is 40 meters. Multiplying these two dimensions gives us an area of 3200 square meters.",
      "template_data": {
        "equation_steps": [
          "Area of Rectangle = Length × Width",
          "Area of Rectangle = 80 m × 40 m",
          "Area of Rectangle = 3200 m²"
        ],
        "animation_style": "stagger_in"
      },
      "audio_url": "./scene_6.wav"
